# One line. Run from the repo root by `orgasmic verify TASK-JK66P`.
# `env -u ...` because a dispatch leaks its run id and home into subprocesses,
# and these tests build and drive a supervisor that must see neither.
#
# Two tests, because MRJRK's incident has two observables and the injection
# takes both: the healthy worker is released (the kill), and its tombstone says
# only `stall_timeout_exceeded` (the operator, told nothing). Neither sits
# through the production 600s window — both compress it to 1s through
# `stall_timeout_secs`, the same field production resolves from
# `DEFAULT_STALL_TIMEOUT`.
env -u ORGASMIC_RUN_ID -u ORGASMIC_HOME cargo test -p orgasmic-daemon --lib -- a_silent_pane_with_live_work_under_it_is_never_stalled the_stall_reason_names_the_evidence_that_was_absent
